# Environment Variables in Deployment

Keep `.env`, Kubernetes configs, and Docker files in sync.

## Source of Truth

`.env.example` is the canonical list of environment variables.

## Kubernetes ConfigMap

When adding new env vars, update `deploy/kubernetes/bot-army-configmap.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: bot-army-config
  namespace: bot-army
data:
  NATS_HOST: "nats"
  NATS_PORT: "4222"
  PONDER_INTERVAL_MINUTES: "5"
  # Add new variables here with sensible defaults
```

## Kubernetes Deployment

Reference ConfigMap in `deploy/kubernetes/bot-army-deployment.yaml`:

```yaml
env:
  - name: NATS_HOST
    valueFrom:
      configMapKeyRef:
        name: bot-army-config
        key: NATS_HOST
```

For secrets (API keys, passwords), use Kubernetes Secrets instead:

```yaml
env:
  - name: CLAUDE_API_KEY
    valueFrom:
      secretKeyRef:
        name: bot-army-secrets
        key: claude-api-key
```

## Dockerfile

Pass build-time args for values needed during build:

```dockerfile
ARG NATS_HOST=localhost
ENV NATS_HOST=${NATS_HOST}
```

## Checklist

When adding a new environment variable:
- [ ] Added to `.env.example` with description
- [ ] Added to `deploy/kubernetes/bot-army-configmap.yaml` (or Secrets for sensitive values)
- [ ] Referenced in `deploy/kubernetes/bot-army-deployment.yaml`
- [ ] Documented in `deploy/README.md`
